**Findings**

P2 [src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1847](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1847): `flush_text` still only preserves `pre` when recovery succeeds. After `flush_tool` folds malformed wrapped content into `text` at [line 1869](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1869), any later TEXT segment is appended to the same buffer at [line 1888](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1888). If recovery finds a call, `tx=pre` drops all text after the first recovered call before pushing calls. So “malformed wrapper then text” can lose the later text and cannot maintain full model-order output.

